    },
    "body": "This records the owner's comprehensive source review and clarified geometric language-model direction: no serving matrix products or transformer backbone, permitted geometric address/page lookup, and shared typed operators as the current priority. Expert gates remain a conditional future option under the owner's later clarification; offline Rust training may use matmul.\n\nThe source-linked review covers native and historical engines, prime/angular routing, zeta/RH/spin/calculus/fiber/bundle work, UOR/Prism/matmul, NEMESIS, W33, GoldSnnail, GNAF, SpiralCore and the separate Studio. It distinguishes implemented operations, retained behavior, placeholders, incompatible whole engines and reusable pieces. A 98-entry source map binds referenced files; the local companion inventories all 14,288 tracked paths without claiming a line-by-line proof audit.\n\nThe recommendation is the current Rust geometric model with exact addressed memory, learned contextual transitions and shared typed operators. The next concrete implementation is joint numeric/word/NoRead choice before execution, preserving the distinct NoOperation/NoRead semantics, followed by reusable language emission and composition. d59070c2 and all earlier evidence remain unchanged. The Studio must ultimately run that same model; its current transformer/template paths are not native-model evidence.\n\nValidation: existing architecture-policy check, claim-wording check, JSON parsing/source digests, local report links and git diff whitespace checks pass. The existing policy checker checks its established fields; new clarification fields are documented/parsed, not new enforcement code. No Rust source changes, builds, training, inference, proof campaign or historical model replay. Cumulative model time remains 3,605.626/4,170 seconds. Existing source/user material and artifacts are preserved.\n\nRefs #820, #973, #1139, #1140. No capability issue is closed by this documentation review.\n",
